{"title":"Hook Length Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Introduction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introduction</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Examples\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Examples</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introduction\">Introduction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hook_Length_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Introduction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The hook length theorem is a theorem to used on standard Young tableau. A Young tableau is a left-justified collection of a finite number of blocks such that the number of blocks in each row is weakly decreasing (non-increasing); they are filled with distinct entries. A standard Young tableau is one that satisfies that the entries in each row are increasing from left to right and the entries in each column are increasing from top to bottom.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Tableau.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/db/Tableau.png/200px-Tableau.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"135\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/db/Tableau.png/300px-Tableau.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/d/db/Tableau.png/400px-Tableau.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Above: Example of a tabaleau without entries filled in\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Young_Tableau.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/41/Young_Tableau.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"150\" height=\"90\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Above: Example of a standard Young tabaleau filled in with the numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e291fb78d9fd2a2b6d47a324b1dca5817ea0d5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1-10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Theorem\">Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hook_Length_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>Let the number of cells in a Young tableau be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Define a hook length of a block to be the number of blocks to the right and below the block, including the block.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/7/e07ccde14bf8f9909e2dffb32cc376e7d334db58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h(i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"33\" height=\"20\" /> denote the hook length of a block <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe hook length theorem states that the number of ways to fill a standard Young tableau with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> blocks given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> distinct, arbitrary entries for which to fill it is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/1/301954d7320c786c6185b602289bd50a80e3b60c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{n!}{\\prod h(i) }\\]\" width=\"51\" height=\"42\" />\nwhere we take the product over all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> distinct blocks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> in the grid.\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hook_Length_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Hook_Example.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/08/Hook_Example.png/200px-Hook_Example.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"136\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/08/Hook_Example.png/300px-Hook_Example.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/08/Hook_Example.png/400px-Hook_Example.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Above: A block with hook length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:TableauHook.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f0/TableauHook.png/200px-TableauHook.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"200\" height=\"135\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f0/TableauHook.png/300px-TableauHook.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f0/TableauHook.png/400px-TableauHook.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Above: A standard Young tableau where each block is labeled with its hook length\n</p><p>In the latter example, the number of SYTs is given by the hook length theorem to be \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6ac3ec8b409a70cc0e239c6b5061e37665ae7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{13!}{9\\times7\\times6\\times3\\times2\\times1\\times5\\times3\\times2\\times4\\times2\\times1\\times1} = 11440\\]\" width=\"455\" height=\"38\" />\nsince there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> total blocks.\n</p>\n<h1><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hook_Length_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h1>\n<p>Prove that for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34b14075e86e6e07f2618bbf8c6ec9ff6ae9822f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(k^2)!\\cdot\\displaystyle\\prod_{j=0}^{k-1}\\frac{j!}{(j+k)!}\\]\" width=\"137\" height=\"52\" />is an integer. (2016 USAMO P2)\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018090513\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.029 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.104 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 81/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2522/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:23066:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018090513 and revision id 279717. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}